From: ACK72 <acikom72@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:15:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: wait twenty intervals before reporting beacon loss

The STA beacon monitor reported beacon loss after seven missed intervals,
about 0.77 s with HZ=100. mac80211 then sends two nullfunc frames back to
back and disconnects locally if neither is acknowledged.

APs can skip beacons for more than a second while off channel and keep
serving the station, so those gaps cost a reconnect and several seconds of
outage. Wait twenty intervals, about 2.2 s at 100 TU, which is close to the
limit other clients apply. Losing the AP is still detected, about 1.4 s
later.

Signed-off-by: ACK72 <acikom72@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/mt76.h b/mt76.h
index 2739552f..8b0cf4ab 100644
--- a/mt76.h
+++ b/mt76.h
@@ -376,7 +376,7 @@ enum mt76_wcid_flags {
 };
 
 #define MT76_N_WCIDS 1088
-#define MT76_BEACON_MON_MAX_MISS	7
+#define MT76_BEACON_MON_MAX_MISS	20
 
 /* stored in ieee80211_tx_info::hw_queue */
 #define MT_TX_HW_QUEUE_PHY		GENMASK(3, 2)
